      "cooked": "<p>I can’t remember what environment card said this, or which environment deck it was even from, but it stated something to the effect that it could be destroyed by discarding one ongoing card.</p>\n<p>I’ve always taken discard to mean remove from hand, while removing anything from play is known as destroying.  Does this mean that a player would have to take an ongoing card from his hand into the trash to destroy this environment card?</p>",
